==={{FloorNumber|uk=0|caps=y|nohelp=y}}===
The {{FloorNumber|uk=0}} is the floor players enter right when they enter the building.

On this floor are red doors, level 3 [[zombie rat]]s, and level 1 [[rat]]s, as well as various decorations to give the building an abandoned look. The north-east room contains an exit that will take players to basement and then outside on the building's east side. To proceed, players must kill the small zombie rat with a long tail to get a [[Key (Melzar's Maze)#Red|red key]]. Players can then open the '''north-west door''', climbing the ladder to the next floor.

==={{FloorNumber|uk=1|caps=y|nohelp=y}}===
On the {{FloorNumber|uk=1}}, players will have to fight level 19 [[Ghost (Melzar's Maze)|ghost]]s. To proceed, players must kill the capeless, hooded ghost to get an [[Key (Melzar's Maze)#Orange|orange key]]. Players can then open the '''second north-east door''', climbing the ladder to reach the top floor.

==={{FloorNumber|uk=2|caps=y|nohelp=y}}===
On the {{FloorNumber|uk=2}}, players will have to fight level 22 [[Skeleton (Melzar's Maze)|skeleton]]s. To proceed, players must kill the skeleton with the small, round shield to get a [[Key (Melzar's Maze)#Yellow|yellow key]]. Players can then open the '''south-west door''' and continue down the hallway to the ladder, descending several ladders to reach the basement, the toughest part of the maze.

===Basement===
As soon as a player lands in the basement, they will notice two level 24 [[Zombie (Melzar's Maze)|zombie]]s, a brown door, and a blue door. The brown door leads to an exit, while the blue door leads to the next enemy in the maze. Players must kill the zombies until they receive a [[Key (Melzar's Maze)#Blue|blue key]] in order to proceed through the only available blue door.<!-- I think this may be discernable through Monster Inspect, in the rare case anyone wants to farm the blue keys. -->

Behind the blue door is [[Melzar the Mad]] (level 43). When players attack him, he will use [[Melee]] as well as [[Magic]] attacks. He will also sometimes make [[cabbage]] pop up nearby. In this room, the brown door leads to an exit, but the magenta door, which is opened via the [[Key (Melzar's Maze)#Magenta|magenta key]] obtained from Melzar, leads to the last opponent in Melzar's Maze.

Behind the magenta door is a [[Lesser demon (Melzar's Maze)|lesser demon]] (level 82). There is a safespot for players using ranged or magic and a strategy to avoid damage for players using melee as well. Mages and rangers can stand one square to the right of the magenta door when looking north (this spot can also be used with a halberd). Players using melee can lure the demon to the western part of the room, and attack it at his maximum attack range then walk one square west to make it lose interest, repeating that strategy as many times as needed. Once slain, it will drop the [[Key (Melzar's Maze)#Green|green key]], which can be used to open the green door, accessing the chest containing the map part required in [[Dragon Slayer I]].

